    "collapsible_tabs_UDrTRf": {
      "type": "collapsible-tabs",
      "blocks": {
        "content_aq3BG8": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What is a GVM upgrade and why do I need one?",
            "content": "<p>Gross Vehicle Mass (GVM) is the maximum your Chevy Silverado 1500 can legally weigh when fully loaded—including the truck, passengers, fuel, accessories (like bull bars and canopies), and tow ball weight. If you are towing heavy or building a touring rig, the factory payload gets eaten up fast. Our GVM upgrades legally increase this limit so you can carry your gear without voiding your insurance or risking hefty fines.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_97RYwd": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "What does \"Pre-Rego\" and \"SSM Approval\" mean?",
            "content": "<p>SSM stands for Second Stage of Manufacture. When we upgrade your truck <em>before</em> it is registered for the very first time (Pre-Rego), the federal government recognizes ORI as the secondary manufacturer. This means your massive lift, larger tyres, and upgraded GVM are baked into the truck's federal compliance plate. It is 100% legal to drive and insure in every state and territory in Australia.<br/><br/></p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_k7yrdM": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Will upgrading my GVM reduce my towing capacity?",
            "content": "<p>Not with an ORI package. Some GVM upgrades force you to sacrifice towing capacity to carry more weight in the tub. Our Chevy Silverado 1500 packages hold the full 4500kg braked towing capacity on every stage except Stage 2, which is rated to 4200kg, while lifting Gross Combined Mass from the factory 7160kg to as much as 8750kg.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        },
        "content_rQQeBN": {
          "type": "content",
          "settings": {
            "icon": "none",
            "title": "Are 35-inch tyres actually legal on these builds?",
            "content": "<p>Yes. Our Stage 4 and Stage 5 SSM packages are federally engineered for 295/70 R18 or 35x12.5 R18 tyres, certified as part of the build when done Pre-Rego. No state-based engineering headaches, just turn the key and drive it legally anywhere in the country.</p>",
            "custom_liquid": "",
            "content_page": "",
            "open": false
          }
        }
      },
